## Usage
Use the MCP tool `dev-swarm.request` to send the payload as a JSON string:

```json
{"server_id":"dart","tool_name":"get_widget_properties","arguments":{"widget_id":"root"}}
```

## Tool Description
Retrieves properties for a specific widget identified by its id. Requires "connect_dart_tooling_daemon" to be successfully called first.

## Arguments Schema
The schema below describes the `arguments` object in the request payload.
```json
{
  "type": "object",
  "properties": {
    "widget_id": {
      "type": "string",
      "description": "The id of the widget to inspect"
    }
  },
  "required": ["widget_id"]
}
```

## Background Tasks
If the tool returns a task id, poll the task status via the MCP request tool:

```json
{"server_id":"dart","method":"tasks/status","params":{"task_id":"<task_id>"}}
```

